; Axis D (variant discriminant) — a default that selects NO variant.
;
; `prim` is discriminated on `:topology`, which defaults to `tri-list`;
; the only variant is gated on the two strips. The author writes
; `(prim :strip-format uint16)` — no `:topology`. With axis D on the
; overlay yields `topology = tri-list`, which SATISFIES the discriminant
; (the form has a value; it just gains no variant keys) — so no
; `missing_discriminant_key` — and `:strip-format` is `unknown_key`
; exactly as it would be had the author written `:topology tri-list`.
;
; This pins a fix: the overlay pre-resolution used to mark the
; discriminant satisfied only when its default also selected a variant,
; so a default outside every variant reported the discriminant missing on
; a form that had one. `effective-axis-d-default-selects-variant` is the
; sibling where the default does select.
(plugin :name gfx :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name topo :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set :values [tri-list tri-strip line-list line-strip]))
  (form :name prim :discriminant topology
    (key :name topology :type topo :optional true :default tri-list)
    (variant :when [tri-strip line-strip]
      (key :name strip-format :type symbol :optional true))))

(prim :strip-format uint16)
